// E0444: a `.plyx` built by a different binary.
//
// The header carries the container format and digests of the compiler and the
// runtime that built it, and a run refuses an artifact that disagrees with any of
// the three before it decodes a body:
//
//   $ ply-0.12 build artifact_version.ply -o app.plyx
//   $ ply-0.13 run app.plyx
//   E0444  the artifact is format 6 and this `ply` writes and reads format 7
//          = rebuild the artifact with this `ply`; re-transferring it will not help
//
// Its own code and not `E0443` because the responses are opposite: a version
// mismatch is rebuilt, a corrupt transfer is re-sent. Telling a deployment to
// re-transfer a file that will never verify is how an incident lasts an hour.
//
// The standard library definitions it draws on are its own, carried by hash like
// the rest, so a `ply` that ships other ones runs it as it was built.

pub fn shade(n: Int) -> Int = n + n

fn main() -> Int = shade(21)
